{
  "dom_id": "step-q133920",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/b5d153746d837a857918028aceb623a5c2b9267f00b6baaceb2f24a8172587ee.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nUse the trend line to predict the value of $y$ when $x=70.$",
  "worked_solution": "To make our prediction, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we start at $x=70$ on the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/6a45fb7d9e609ac872996f1f8ad6ea311369ae328064fac68ca21ee71a079b49.png)\n\n* Then, we move up until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/b21720b002061d922f8b8de8a09ed9d229c396ea61a893c8042fba716119415c.png)\n\n- Finally, we move left until we intersect the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/3c26887cf68b1e34a316506b96bb0cc9f634acb894f6fd7c216c38fffac9e752.png)\n\nTherefore, when $x=70,$ we obtain $y≈5.$",
